meta {
  name: Review Offline Token Payment (College Admin)
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/college-admin/payments/offline/{{offlineTransactionId}}/review
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{staffAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "decision": "verified",
    "received_amount": 25000
  }
}

docs {
  Marks an offline token payment submission as received ("verified") or
  rejected. `decision`: "verified" | "rejected".

  Double-entry verification: when marking "verified", staff must manually
  type the amount actually received (`received_amount`) — it must exactly
  match the course's configured token_amount, or this 409s
  ("The received amount must exactly match the configured token amount")
  without finalizing anything. This is a deliberate re-check step, not a
  rubber-stamp of whatever the student submitted.

  When marking "rejected", `note` is required — becomes the transaction's
  rejection_reason, shown to the student so they can resubmit.

  On "verified" success: Transaction.status -> "completed",
  verification_status -> "verified", amount overwritten with the
  staff-entered received_amount, paid_at/verified_by/verified_at set,
  StudentFeeLedger -> "paid", ApplicationCourse.status -> "token_paid",
  the linked OfferLetter updated, and a payment receipt is generated
  asynchronously (same invoice job as the online flow).

  On "rejected": only verification_status/rejection_reason change —
  nothing about the course/offer is touched, the student can resubmit.

  404 if the transaction doesn't exist or isn't currently
  "pending_verification" (e.g. already reviewed).
}
